    {
      "bbox": [
        147,
        1315,
        1643,
        1682
      ],
      "category": "Text",
      "text": "b. If, after expiration of the ten (10) day period, the labor organization making the request is still shown to be the authorized representative of at least thirty (30) percent of the employees involved and no good reason appears for not acting upon the request, the Commissioner of Labor will proceed to arrange for the conduct of a fair and free secret-ballot election. Any other labor organization desiring to participate in the election will be permitted to do so if it makes timely response to the notice and submits evidence showing that it is the authorized representative of at least ten (10) percent of the employees involved.",
